## Context
Skill bodies carry history that the rules say belongs in memory and tickets (`rules/git.md`, `rules/workflow.md`). Counts on origin/main at 95dfc077, grep for `ticket NNNN`: gaze 16, roar 5, molt 5, raid 4; also dated incident notes and runtime-version pins (for example "Claude Code 2.1.218") in gaze, email, roar, raid, infrastructure, submission-event, molt, yawn. These cost tokens on every run and go stale.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Each rule keeps its imperative; the incident or ticket number behind it moves to the ticket or a memory note, or is dropped
- [ ] Version pins removed, or replaced by a behaviour statement a test can check
- [ ] Byte-compare of the rendered catalog unchanged except for intended edits
- [ ] gaze is handled after 1100 child 2 so the two edits do not collide

